<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayadhwaj Singha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1648">1648</a>–<a href="/years/1663">1663</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sutamla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayadhwaj Singha was king of the Ahom kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> from 1648 to 1663 and the first Ahom king to take initiation from a Vaishnavite satra. In 1662 the Mughal governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, Mir Jumla, invaded, occupied the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhgaon">Garhgaon</a> and forced him into the hills, and in 1663 he accepted the harsh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-ghilajharighat">Treaty of Ghilajharighat</a>, which imposed tribute and the loss of western territory. He died soon afterwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jayadhwaj-singha.jpg" alt="Jayadhwaj Singha" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ComparingQuantities · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jayadhwaj_Singha_with_Banamali_dev.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
